WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:02.299
(rhythmic music)

00:00:02.299 --> 00:00:04.545
(elevator pings)

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:05.769
- Here it is, fourth floor.

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:06.602
- Oh, thanks.

00:00:06.602 --> 00:00:08.222
- Once again, Mr.
O'Brien, it is so exciting

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:09.690
to have you here in San Diego.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.083
I'm a big fan of
entertainment of all kinds.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:14.037
This is kinda the biggest
celebrity we've had here

00:00:14.037 --> 00:00:17.528
since I think Comic-Con
2007, Michael Chiklis.

00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:18.407
He's great.

00:00:18.407 --> 00:00:19.256
- He's very good.

00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:20.339
- You know, some people like the Hulk,

00:00:20.339 --> 00:00:21.685
but I'm a Thing man myself.

00:00:21.685 --> 00:00:22.518
- Oh, okay.

00:00:22.518 --> 00:00:23.836
- And I do think you have to choose.

00:00:23.836 --> 00:00:26.354
You hear some people say, "I
like the Hulk and the Thing."

00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:27.696
Take a position, you know.

00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:28.529
- [Conan] Yeah.
- Hey, while you're here,

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:29.974
you gotta go to the naval base.

00:00:29.974 --> 00:00:31.640
You gotta do that, promise
me you're gonna do that.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.473
- I don't know if we'll have time.

00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:34.363
- And SeaWorld, you gotta go to SeaWorld.

00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:35.196
(audience laughs)

00:00:35.196 --> 00:00:37.451
You probably heard they
got rid of the whales.

00:00:37.451 --> 00:00:38.549
- Yeah, I did hear that.

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:39.382
(audience laughs)

00:00:39.382 --> 00:00:40.621
- It's so sad because
what are those whales

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:41.758
gonna do now, you know?

00:00:41.758 --> 00:00:43.383
There's not a lot of
opportunities for whales.

00:00:43.383 --> 00:00:44.216
(audience laughs)
That was

00:00:44.216 --> 00:00:45.049
a good job for a whale.

00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:46.879
Hey, you know where else you
can go though, is Legoland.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.016
Have you been to Legoland?

00:00:48.016 --> 00:00:49.074
- [Conan] Uh, no, I've never been there.

00:00:49.074 --> 00:00:50.251
- [Bellhop] Okay, well,
here is the problem.

00:00:50.251 --> 00:00:52.569
You literally cannot get
in there if you're an adult

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:53.830
just going alone without a kid.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:54.663
They won't let you in.

00:00:54.663 --> 00:00:55.759
(audience laughs)
Isn't that crazy?

00:00:55.759 --> 00:00:57.868
You're thrown into a position
to have to find a kid

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.020
so you can get in, and
I can find you a kid.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.604
Like, if you need a kid
to get into Legoland,

00:01:01.604 --> 00:01:02.901
- No, I don't want a kid
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.657
- I have a lead on two different kids.

00:01:04.657 --> 00:01:06.199
One of them is getting a little old but...

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.032
- Okay.

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:07.865
I'd rather not know about it.

00:01:07.865 --> 00:01:08.698
- He looks young.

00:01:08.698 --> 00:01:10.368
(audience laughs)
And here is your room.

00:01:10.368 --> 00:01:11.201
- This is it?

00:01:11.201 --> 00:01:12.097
- This is it.

00:01:12.097 --> 00:01:13.886
- We got off the elevator right there.

00:01:13.886 --> 00:01:14.878
(audience laughs)
- That's right.

00:01:14.878 --> 00:01:16.140
You're gonna be right by the elevator.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.929
- So why did we go all the way?

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:20.044
- Oh, the cart isn't great
with left-hand turns.

00:01:20.044 --> 00:01:20.978
I just preferred to do a right.

00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:22.078
(audience laughs)

00:01:22.078 --> 00:01:23.300
A little bit of circle.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.194
- I, I'm really tired.

00:01:24.194 --> 00:01:25.091
I'd just love to get inside.

00:01:25.091 --> 00:01:26.150
- You must be tired, yeah.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.043
- Yeah.

00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:28.184
- Do you have a key?

00:01:28.184 --> 00:01:29.017
(audience laughs)
- Yeah.

00:01:29.017 --> 00:01:30.747
- A lot of the bellhops
have keys that they can get

00:01:30.747 --> 00:01:32.535
into all the rooms, but they
don't give me one anymore.

00:01:32.535 --> 00:01:33.368
I had one.

00:01:33.368 --> 00:01:34.201
- What did you do?

00:01:34.201 --> 00:01:36.073
- It's not something I'm super proud of.

00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:37.681
(audience laughs)
- Um, your name again is, is?

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:38.514
- [Bellhop] It's Frederick.

00:01:38.514 --> 00:01:39.347
- Frederick.

00:01:39.347 --> 00:01:40.431
- Hey listen, if you need anything,

00:01:40.431 --> 00:01:43.199
just pick up your phone,
dial nine and then star.

00:01:43.199 --> 00:01:44.032
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:44.032 --> 00:01:45.716
- And then seven, seven, and then hang up

00:01:45.716 --> 00:01:47.713
and then pick it up again
and then nine again.

00:01:47.713 --> 00:01:48.546
(audience laughs)

00:01:48.546 --> 00:01:51.209
And then three or four six's,

00:01:51.209 --> 00:01:53.683
and then wait like a minute
and I should pick up,

00:01:53.683 --> 00:01:55.757
unless I'm on my break or
unless that doesn't work.

00:01:55.757 --> 00:01:56.590
It might not work.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.504
- I'm just gonna go in.

00:01:57.504 --> 00:01:59.289
- [Frederick] Uh, yeah, all right, yeah.

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:00.122
Have a good night's sleep.

00:02:00.122 --> 00:02:00.956
You're gonna like this room.

00:02:00.956 --> 00:02:03.152
- Terrific, thank you so
much, and we'll see you later.

00:02:03.152 --> 00:02:04.083
- Yeah, you want me to
come in and help you

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:05.428
turn on your fireplace or anything?

00:02:05.428 --> 00:02:06.261
- No, I got it myself.

00:02:06.261 --> 00:02:07.094
- Are you sure?

00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:07.927
- Thank you.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.760
- [Frederick] Have a good night's sleep!

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.493
- We're good.

00:02:10.493 --> 00:02:11.457
(exhales)

00:02:11.457 --> 00:02:14.624
(slow dramatic music)

00:02:17.475 --> 00:02:18.737
(fire blazing)

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:21.654
(audience laughs)

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:26.270
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.103
(audience laughs)

00:02:46.597 --> 00:02:49.430
(audience laughs)

00:02:51.079 --> 00:02:55.079
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.977
(audience laughs)

00:03:19.121 --> 00:03:22.038
(audience laughs)

00:03:24.528 --> 00:03:25.797
(door knocking)

00:03:25.797 --> 00:03:26.814
(audience laughs)

00:03:26.814 --> 00:03:28.153
- Hi, sorry to bug you, but I thought

00:03:28.153 --> 00:03:29.862
you might like some ice.

00:03:29.862 --> 00:03:31.815
- Uh, I think I'm good, thank you.

00:03:31.815 --> 00:03:34.174
- Hey, this really does a
great job keeping things cold.

00:03:34.174 --> 00:03:36.653
- That's what ice is kind of famous for,

00:03:36.653 --> 00:03:38.196
but I think I don't need ice.

00:03:38.196 --> 00:03:40.642
- Okay, sorry to bother you.

00:03:40.642 --> 00:03:41.985
(slow dramatic music)

00:03:41.985 --> 00:03:42.878
(audience laughs)

00:03:42.878 --> 00:03:44.787
(door knocking)

00:03:44.787 --> 00:03:45.704
Toblerone!

00:03:46.614 --> 00:03:49.094
- I'm, I'm really not a
Toblerone guy, but thank you.

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:49.927
- Are you sure?

00:03:49.927 --> 00:03:51.817
This is from my own private stash.

00:03:51.817 --> 00:03:53.524
- [Conan] I know but thank you.

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:55.557
Just thanks very much.

00:03:55.557 --> 00:03:56.820
(slow dramatic music)

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.961
(door knocking)

00:03:57.961 --> 00:03:59.497
Son of a bitch!

00:03:59.497 --> 00:04:00.717
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.717 --> 00:04:01.550
- You know what this is.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:02.383
Do you need it?

00:04:02.383 --> 00:04:04.222
- (sighs) I, no.

00:04:04.222 --> 00:04:06.298
I'm just gonna go number one, okay, so...

00:04:06.298 --> 00:04:09.183
- Just number one all night long?

00:04:09.183 --> 00:04:10.120
Hey, Mr. O'Brien.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:10.953
- Look,

00:04:10.953 --> 00:04:11.786
(audience laughs)

00:04:11.786 --> 00:04:12.678
I do these shows.

00:04:12.678 --> 00:04:14.628
I'm tired and I need to sleep.

00:04:14.628 --> 00:04:15.729
(door shuts)

00:04:15.729 --> 00:04:18.815
(audience laughs)

00:04:18.815 --> 00:04:19.648
- Oops.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:22.560
- You're sure I have to go all the way

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.946
to the lobby for a new key?

00:04:23.946 --> 00:04:25.571
- Yeah, that's policy.

00:04:25.571 --> 00:04:26.404
(Conan groans)

00:04:26.404 --> 00:04:27.642
You have an ID, right?

00:04:27.642 --> 00:04:29.348
- No, I don't have ID.

00:04:29.348 --> 00:04:30.652
- Ah, that's all right.

00:04:30.652 --> 00:04:31.973
Everybody knows that face.

00:04:31.973 --> 00:04:34.890
(audience laughs)

